cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SafetyPulse, please cite it as below."
title: "SafetyPulse: Catching Safety Drift During Fine-Tuning by Reading the Model's Refusal Circuit"
abstract: >-
  An early-warning signal for safety drift during LLM fine-tuning. A Circuit Integrity Score, read from the model's
  refusal circuit on 50 prompt pairs, flags every unsafe held-out checkpoint before harm becomes measurable; a
  SafeTune low-rank restore repairs the drift. Built on Cohere Labs' Tiny Aya Global for the Lexsi Labs AI Safety &
  Alignment Hackathon (Track 2b).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Purvansh
    family-names: Joshi
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/PxA-Labs/safetypulse"
url: "https://huggingface.co/blog/purvansh01/safetypulse-safety-drift-monitor"
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - llm-safety
  - fine-tuning
  - mechanistic-interpretability
  - safety-monitoring
  - model-repair
